WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.037 --> 00:00:05.430
Edward's heart pounded as he sat up and looked around the stall.

2
00:00:05.431 --> 00:00:09.069
He couldn't see what had touched him in the dark.

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:14.919
"Who's there?" Edward called out nervously, but again no one answered.

4
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.193
"Whoever you are, reveal yourself.

5
00:00:18.194 --> 00:00:24.068
And if you're a ghost, well . . . I'm not afraid of ghosts!"

6
00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:27.105
Edward sounded much braver than he felt.

7
00:00:27.106 --> 00:00:32.316
He wished that the mysterious creature would go away and leave him alone.

8
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:37.135
But it startled him again, this time by slapping his arm.

9
00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:40.276
"Stop that!" Edward cried out.

10
00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:45.441
There was only one thing to do: touch the creature before it touched him again.

11
00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:51.275
Edward reached out a trembling hand and touched a long, warm tail.

12
00:00:51.276 --> 00:00:57.704
"You're not a ghost!" Edward laughed with relief.

13
00:00:57.705 --> 00:01:06.927
"You're just a calf! Lie down beside me, and we'll keep each other warm."

14
00:01:06.928 --> 00:01:11.113
With his new friend nearby, Edward felt less lonely.

15
00:01:11.114 --> 00:01:18.515
As he fell asleep, he thought about how relieved he was to be free of John and Frank.

16
00:01:18.516 --> 00:01:23.219
The next morning Edward was leaving the stall when he heard someone humming.

17
00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:29.220
Before he could hide, a little girl carrying a basket entered the barn.

18
00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:33.763
Her eyes widened with surprise when she spotted Edward.

19
00:01:33.764 --> 00:01:40.055
"You don't belong here," she said. "Who are you?"

20
00:01:40.056 --> 00:01:45.996
"I'm Edward, your king. Who are you?"

21
00:01:45.997 --> 00:01:52.213
"My name is Priscilla Grant, and I'm honored to meet you, Your Majesty."

22
00:01:52.214 --> 00:01:56.312
Priscilla put down her basket and curtsied to Edward.

23
00:01:56.313 --> 00:01:59.598
Edward was surprised at this mark of respect.

24
00:01:59.599 --> 00:02:03.710
People usually mocked him when he announced he was king.

25
00:02:03.711 --> 00:02:08.215
"What are you doing in our barn?" Priscilla asked.

26
00:02:08.216 --> 00:02:14.160
"We have cows and horses sleeping here, but you're our first king."

27
00:02:14.161 --> 00:02:19.007
Edward told Priscilla everything that had happened since he left the palace.

28
00:02:19.008 --> 00:02:24.265
"I can't remember the last time I had a good meal," he said.

29
00:02:24.266 --> 00:02:30.152
"We don't have much, but my mother always feeds beggars," Priscilla said.

30
00:02:30.153 --> 00:02:34.416
"Come with me."

31
00:02:34.417 --> 00:02:39.577
As he followed Priscilla to the farmhouse, Edward made a silent vow.

32
00:02:39.578 --> 00:02:48.916
"After I'm crowned, I'll always be kind to children because Priscilla helped me."

33
00:02:48.917 --> 00:02:54.536
Mrs. Grant was surprised to have a king in her kitchen, but she welcomed Edward.

34
00:02:54.537 --> 00:02:59.843
"I pity the boy," she thought as she listened to his story.

35
00:02:59.844 --> 00:03:02.765
"There's something wrong with his mind.

36
00:03:02.766 --> 00:03:07.694
I'll find out where he belongs and send him home."

37
00:03:07.695 --> 00:03:13.026
Mrs. Grant gave Edward a large chunk of bread and told him to sit by the fire.

38
00:03:13.027 --> 00:03:19.030
"That's all I have right now, but lunch will be ready at noon."

39
00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:24.090
She watched the boy for a moment, wondering if he lived outside.

40
00:03:24.091 --> 00:03:28.826
Perhaps he was a shepherd.

41
00:03:28.827 --> 00:03:34.979
"So, Priscilla found you in our barn." Mrs. Grant stirred some soup.

42
00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.511
"Do you have much experience with animals?"

43
00:03:39.512 --> 00:03:43.516
"No, not really." Edward swallowed some bread.

44
00:03:43.517 --> 00:03:49.056
"We have dogs and horses at the palace, but the servants take care of them.”

45
00:03:49.057 --> 00:03:53.069
At the mention of servants, Mrs. Grant had another idea.

46
00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.849
Maybe he was a servant.

47
00:03:55.850 --> 00:04:01.129
She talked about carrying firewood, scrubbing floors, and polishing boots.

48
00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:06.118
But Edward didn't have anything to say about those things.

49
00:04:06.119 --> 00:04:11.091
Mrs. Grant moved on to breaking eggs.

50
00:04:11.092 --> 00:04:14.764
"You should see our head chef break eggs for chocolate cake!"

51
00:04:14.765 --> 00:04:17.793
Edward said enthusiastically.

52
00:04:17.794 --> 00:04:20.775
"She never drops any shells in the batter.

53
00:04:20.776 --> 00:04:24.626
And she makes the best pies and . . ."

54
00:04:24.627 --> 00:04:29.027
Mrs. Grant smiled as Edward described his favorite desserts.

55
00:04:29.028 --> 00:04:34.533
"He's eaten a lot of fancy foods," she thought.

56
00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:39.368
"He must be a kitchen helper, maybe even in the palace.

57
00:04:39.369 --> 00:04:45.381
I'll test him by having him wash dishes."

58
00:04:45.382 --> 00:04:49.536
"Dishes? You want me to wash dishes?"

59
00:04:49.537 --> 00:04:55.276
At first Edward was insulted, but then he remembered the family's kindness to him.

60
00:04:55.277 --> 00:04:59.763
Washing dishes might be a way to thank them.

61
00:04:59.764 --> 00:05:07.266
After Edward finished the dishes—he broke a cup and a plate—Mrs. Grant had more chores for him.

62
00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:13.943
That morning he learned to peel apples, sharpen knives, and sweep the kitchen floor.

63
00:05:13.944 --> 00:05:20.305
He didn't do a great job with any of these chores, but Mrs. Grant still gave him lunch.

64
00:05:20.306 --> 00:05:24.186
After lunch Edward was eager to be on his way.

65
00:05:24.187 --> 00:05:30.003
However, Mrs. Grant had other ideas and handed him a pail full of kitchen scraps.

66
00:05:30.004 --> 00:05:35.301
"Oh, I don't need more food." Edward tried to hand the pail back to her.

67
00:05:35.302 --> 00:05:38.159
"I'm full from lunch."

68
00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.952
Mrs. Grant struggled to hide a smile.

69
00:05:40.953 --> 00:05:46.578
"These are for the pigs, Your Majesty.

70
00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:52.548
Let's go outside, and I'll show you where the pigpen is."

71
00:05:52.549 --> 00:05:56.906
"You've been very kind to me," Edward said as they went outside.

72
00:05:56.907 --> 00:06:00.693
He was about to say that kings don't feed pigs.

73
00:06:00.694 --> 00:06:07.474
But just then he spotted two people coming up the front path—John and Frank!

74
00:06:07.475 --> 00:06:10.771
"Thank you for everything. I must be going!"

75
00:06:10.772 --> 00:06:18.183
Edward dropped the bucket of scraps. "Right now!"

